# Internationalization

Every user-facing string (visible labels, `aria-label`, `title` tooltips, `confirm()` copy, errors, hints, default session/track names) **must** use `t('…')` from `src/lib/i18n`.

- Add new keys to **both** `src/lib/i18n/fr.ts` and `src/lib/i18n/en.ts` (and any future locale files).
- Call `useLocale()` in React components that render translated copy so they re-render when the language changes.
- Do **not** hardcode French or English in components or `sessionActions` / runtime helpers.
- Brand name **PolyRecorder** stays untranslated.
- Language names in the picker stay in their native form (Français, English, …) via the locale catalog, not via `t()`.
- Shortcut key chords (E / R, F2, …) may stay literal.
